# P72 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): a context menu whose first item resets the camera.
# GTK opens the context menu under the pointer, which then hovers Reset the camera and selects it; the AppKit file's Down moved on to Snapshot (2026-10-16, SNAPSHOT logged). Return alone activates it.
# 按鍵次數在 GTK 上實測(2026-10-16)。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let P72 lay out,macos
click,238,518,frame,left,,,stop the clock first so the readout is stable,macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
move,239,284,frame,,,,"onto the mesh view -- added 2026-09-28: Reset the camera sets dist back to 3.40, which is also its launch value, so without moving the camera first the capture (p72-macos-final-20260928-090808.png, dist 3.40, scrolls 0) could not show the menu item had done anything",macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
scroll,0,5,,,,,five notches: the camera comes closer and dist drops below 3.40,macos
